Real-World Significance
This isn't just a CTF trick — it's a well-documented real-world vulnerability:

NSA documents leaked in 2013 (by Edward Snowden) had "redacted" text that was trivially recoverable because the same overlay method was used. 
Court filings in the US and UK have repeatedly had "redacted" personal information (names, addresses, financial data) recovered by journalists and researchers using the exact same copy-paste technique.
